{"name":"Wishing Troll","hex":"#9a834b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wishing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["gerund of wish (“the act of making a wish”)"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of wish"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wishing"},{"term":"troll","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["a giant supernatural being, especially a grotesque humanoid creature living in caves or hills or under bridges. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A type of diminutive supernatural being; a dwarf."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Senses relating to a rolling motion.\n\nTo move (something, especially a round object) by, or as if by, rolling; to bowl, to roll, to trundle. \n\n Often followed by in: to cause (something) to flow or roll in like a stream.\n\nTo roll; also, to turn round and round; to rotate, to spin, to whirl. \n\nTo move or walk at a leisurely pace; to ramble, to saunter, to stroll. \n\n Chiefly of a man: synonym of cruise (“to stroll about to find a (male) sexual partner”). \n Followed by in: to flow or roll in like a stream.","To move (something, especially a round object) by, or as if by, rolling; to bowl, to roll, to trundle. \n\n Often followed by in: to cause (something) to flow or roll in like a stream."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/troll"}],"entries":[{"title":"Troll doll","blocks":[{"text":"A troll doll is a type of plastic doll with furry up-combed hair depicting a troll, also known as a Dam doll after their creator Danish woodcutter Thomas Dam. The inspiration came from trolls in old Scandinavian folklore. The toys are also known as good luck trolls."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/93/Wizard_troll_doll-low_res.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Troll_doll","wikidata":"Q4992093"},{"title":"Troll","blocks":[{"text":"A troll is a being in Nordic folklore, including Norse mythology. In Old Norse sources, beings described as trolls dwell in isolated areas of rocks, mountains, or caves, live together in small family units, and are rarely helpful to human beings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/John_Bauer_1915.jpg/330px-John_Bauer_1915.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Troll","wikidata":"Q12581"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Wall_of_Trolls.jpg/500px-Wall_of_Trolls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Wall_of_Trolls.jpg/1280px-Wall_of_Trolls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Wall_of_Trolls.jpg/500px-Wall_of_Trolls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A collection of troll dolls","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWall_of_Trolls.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Theodor_Kittelsen_-_Forest_Troll_-_NG.K%26H.B.03222_-_National_Museum_of_Art%2C_Architecture_and_Design.jpg/500px-Theodor_Kittelsen_-_Forest_Troll_-_NG.K%26H.B.03222_-_National_Museum_of_Art%2C_Architecture_and_Design.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Theodor_Kittelsen_-_Forest_Troll_-_NG.K%26H.B.03222_-_National_Museum_of_Art%2C_Architecture_and_Design.jpg/1280px-Theodor_Kittelsen_-_Forest_Troll_-_NG.K%26H.B.03222_-_National_Museum_of_Art%2C_Architecture_and_Design.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Theodor_Kittelsen_-_Forest_Troll_-_NG.K%26H.B.03222_-_National_Museum_of